    "passage": "Kyoto is no doubt loved by tourists far and wide. Yet, [[1]] issues upset local Kyoto residents more than tourists overcrowding public places, chatting at high volumes, and littering carelessly. [[2]] overtourism, these are the top three major issues for locals. Other less annoying by-products of excessive tourism include the overloaded transportation system and garbage system, neither of which can [[3]] keep up with the influx of visitors.\nThe local government is taking action to combat these problems. Aside from raising tourism-related tax, the government has been promoting [[4]]. Hopefully, highlighting those hidden gems and sites off the beaten path will reduce overcrowding at certain spots. However, in other cases, the emphasis is on much [[5]] measures, such as banning all outside visitors from the residential neighborhood of Hanami Koji. It is hoped that visitors will learn to be responsible while they are awed by the city’s attractions.",
